 "text": "Treasurer | Riley County Official Website\nSkip To Main Content This website is AudioEye enabled and is being optimized for accessibility. To open the AudioEye Toolbar, press \"shift + =\". Some assistive technologies may require the use of a passthrough function before this keystroke. For more information, activate the button labeled \"Explore your accessibility options\".\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\n-->\nHome\nOur County\nGovernment\nServices\nHow Do I?\nContact Us\nSearch\nMotor Vehicle\nBuying / Selling a Vehicle\nLicensing Your Vehicle\nRefunding a License Plate\nRenewing Your License Plate\nMilitary Requirements\nMotor Vehicle Escrow\nMotor Vehicle Forms\nLicense Plates\nStandard Plates\nMilitary Plates\nDisability Plates\nEducation Plates\nSpecialty Plates\nRecreational Plates\nTaxes\nDelinquent Tax Listings\nIntangible Taxes\nOnline Resources\nPayment Plans\nProperty Taxes\nProtesting Taxes\nReal Estate Taxes\nTax Sales\nContact Us\nIRP/CMV Vehicles\nAccount Requirements\nCommercial Vehicle Forms\nDriver's Licenses\nHome\nGovernment\nDepartments\nTreasurer & Motor Vehicle\nTreasurer\nServices Provided\nMotor vehicles - registration and title\nCollecting taxes\nPlease note, the Treasurer's Office will not process new titles or commercial vehicles after 4:30 pm.\nMake an appointment\nOr call us at (785) 537-6320\nReprint Your Renewal Notice\nThe form will ask you to enter your plate numbers.\nVisit Main DMV for Driver's License Services\nAs of September 2025 all driver's license services, including renewals, tests, and ID cards, will be handled at the Kansas DMV office at 8200 S Port Drive (off HWY 24). Visit the Kansas DMV website here Driver's License Services Visit Main DDriver's License Services Visit Main DMV for Driver's License Services Visit Main DMV for Driver's License Services to make an appointment or call them at (785) 537-2140.\nFAQs\nHow much will it cost to register my vehicle?\nHow can I pay for my tags?\nDo my tags expire on the first day or the last day of the month?\nWhat papers will I need to title a newly-purchased vehicle?\nHow can I renew my tags if I didn't get a renewal notice in the mail?\nI'm moving to Kansas from another state; how do I register my vehicle?\nView All FAQs FAQs\n/FAQ.aspx\nTreasurer Shilo Heger\nEmail the Treasurer's Office\nPhysical Address\n110 Courthouse Plaza\n1st Floor\nManhattan , KS 66502\nPhone: 785-537-6320\nFax: 785-537-6326\nDonna Borgerding\nVehicle Supervisor/ Deputy Treasurer\nHours\nGeneral Services\nMonday - Thursday 7:30 a.m. - 5 p.m.\nFriday 7:30 a.m. - 12 p.m.\nVIN Inspector Hours\nTuesday 7:30 a.m. - 4 p.m.\nWed - Thurs 7:30 a.m. - 2 p.m.\nDirectory\nCommission Meetings\nMotor Vehicles\nDistrict Court\nEmployment\nElection Information\nOnline Payment\n-->\nContact Us\nRiley County Offices\n110 Courthouse Plaza\nManhattan, KS 66502\nPhone: 785-565-6200\nFax: 785-537-6394\nSocial Media\nFacebook\nYoutube\nInstagram\nHelpful Links\nATA Bus\nBurn Permits\nCommission Meetings\nDistrict Court\nDriver's Licenses\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nHelpful Links\nHome\nStaff Directory\nTranslate\nSite Map\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by CivicPlus®\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nClose ×\nOpens in new window\nPDF Download\nWord Download\nExcel Download\nPowerPoint Download\nDocument Download\nExplore your accessibility options",
